  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile + avgpool (config_021, acc=0.591) is the clear best so far, outperforming singleprofile (0.485) and transformer aggregation (0.519). All three completed experiments use pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder, so we have no information about whether a learned encoder (e.g., scgpt) could further improve performance. Question: Does replacing the linear PCA representation with the pre-trained scgpt encoder improve validation accuracy when holding profile (multiprofile) and aggregation (avgpool) fixed at their best-known settings? Why this is the best next step: It is a single-variable change from our strongest result, cleanly isolating the effect of the RNA encoder. If scgpt helps, it justifies further investment in learned representations and multimodal fusion; if it does not, it tells us PCA is sufficient and we should pivot budget toward testing image contributions or fusion strategies. This maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

